ddressbook><name>YOSHIDA, NARIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IGASAKI YASUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYODA HARUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA NARIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IGASAKI, YASUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYODA, HARUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, NARIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A spatial light modulation apparatus using a reflection type spatial light modulator, wherein read light is P-polarized light diagonally entering a light reflecting layer 17, liquid crystals in the light reflecting layer 17 being oriented so that liquid crystal molecules incline, when a voltage is applied by a drive circuit (2), in a plane including both an axis of the read light, incident light, and that of modulated light, outgoing light, i.e. in a plane parallel to a slope.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de modulation spatiale de la lumière utilisant un modulateur spatial de la lumière du type à réflexion, ledit dispositif étant caractérisé en ce que la lumière de lecture est une lumière à polarisation p pénétrant en diagonale dans une couche (17) réfléchissant la lumière, en ce que les cristaux liquides de la couche (17) réfléchissant la lumière sont orientés de manière que les molécules de cristaux liquides soient inclinées, lorsqu'une tension est appliquée par un circuit (2) d'attaque, dans un plan comprenant à la fois l'axe de la lumière de lecture, celui de la lumière incidente, l'axe de la lumière modulée, et celui de la lumière sortante, c'est-à-dire dans un plan parallèle à une pente.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>